WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.900
Every year has a few disasters mixed in with
the masterpieces, and 2017 wasn't any different.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.880
While the year produced some truly great films,
it also had its fair share of clunkers, from

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:16.160
malformed horror movies and badly made bio-pics
to overbearing blockbusters that might just

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.160
give you a migraine.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.700
Here are the worst movies of 2017.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.220
The Snowman

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.640
On paper, The Snowman should've been awesome.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.539
It's headlined by several formidable stars
and was directed by Tomas Alfredson, director

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.780
of well-received films like Let the Right
One In and Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.840
But despite all that talent, this film is
a bloody mess.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:40.520
Based on the novel by Jo Nesbø, The Snowman
follows an alcoholic detective who chases

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.660
a psycho with a thing for building snowmen.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:48.100
Unfortunately, the thrills are undone by a
slew of messy subplots, over-the-top music,

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:53.520
subpar performances, and a bunch of supposedly
freaky Frostys that really aren't that frightening.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:54.960
The Bye Bye Man

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.200
With movies like Split, Get Out, and It Comes

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.400
at Night, 2017 was a pretty solid year for
horror.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.180
But on the flip side, we also got The Bye
Bye Man.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.200
"Bye bye man."

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:12.000
Written by Jonathan Penner and directed by
Stacey Title, this January fright flick has

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.770
been described as "one of the emptiest, nonsensical
haunted thrillers ever to fail genre audiences,"

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:18.560
and for good reason.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.040
As a movie, it fails on every level imaginable,
from the acting to the directing.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.340
And worst of all, the bad guy's mythology
doesn't actually make any sense.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.700
What's up with the coins?

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.080
What's up with the train?

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.060
What's up with the CGI mess of a hellhound?

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.640
So yeah, don't say it.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:34.640
Don't think it.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.900
"Don't say it, don't think it."

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:38.460
"Don't say it, don't think it."

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:39.840
"Don't say it, don't think it."

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.220
And definitely don't watch it.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:42.280
Baywatch

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.300
Based on the hit TV show starring David Hasselhoff

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:48.140
and Pamela Anderson, Baywatch looked pretty
good on paper.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:53.719
It stars Dwayne Johnson and Zac Efron as super-shredded
lifeguards who spend their days saving lives,

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.460
cracking jokes, and fighting crime.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.560
But after Baywatch hit theaters in May 2017,
critics immediately slammed the movie for

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.880
being...well, bad.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.300
So what's up with the hate?

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.680
Maybe it's because the movie focused a little
too much on jokes involving body parts and

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:08.180
fluids.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:12.040
It's not hard to see why critics didn't feel
the need to save this movie from drowning

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.040
at the box office.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.040
Underworld: Blood Wars

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:17.460
Kate Beckinsale has been playing the character

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.440
of Selene since 2003.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.600
In other words, she's been making the Underworld
movies for a long, long time.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.360
It's a shame most of them are terrible.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:30.120
Keeping with tradition, Underworld: Blood
Wars lives up to the franchise's monstrously

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.220
awful reputation.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:37.820
"Roar"
"roar"

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.380
As usual, the plot is "vampires fight werewolves,
and Selene wears a lot of leather."

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:46.770
The directing in uninspired, the dialogue
is stilted, and it may just be the bluest

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:47.680
movie ever made.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.720
In other words, it's probably time to drive
a stake through this franchise's heart and

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.880
let Kate Beckinsale move on to bigger and
better things.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.260
She's killed enough Lycans for one lifetime.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:58.380
The Mummy

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.760
Ever since Iron Man burst onto the screen

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:05.220
in 2008, movie studios have desperately been
trying to copy the Marvel model.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:10.020
Now, we've got the Dark Universe, an attempt
by Universal to cash in on the interconnected

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.400
movie franchise craze.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:16.220
But instead of relying on talking raccoons
or thunder gods, the Dark Universe is reviving

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:20.880
classic movie monsters like the Bride of Frankenstein,
the Invisible Man, and the Mummy.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:25.360
Unfortunately for Universal, they bungled
their whole rebooted universe thing right

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:26.200
out of the gate.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:30.780
The Mummy bombed at the domestic box office,
and the film was savaged by critics.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:36.020
From the opening scene involving Iraqi insurgents
to the undead mummy herself, few critics found

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.180
anything positive to say about the film.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:43.000
Worst of all, The Mummy tried to set up a
cinematic universe in just two hours, whereas

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.440
the MCU unfolded over several movies.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.480
By trying to lay the framework for a future
franchise in just one go, the story suffered.

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:54.540
As a result, The Mummy hasn't done much to
brighten up the future of Universal's Dark

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.260
Universe.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:56.880
The Circle

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.060
With some movies, you can tell right away

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.420
that they're going to be awful.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:03.000
But when some films bomb, it's a little more
surprising.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.020
Take The Circle, for example.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:09.270
It's based on a novel by award-winning author
Dave Eggers, and it features a who's who of

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:13.800
big Hollywood names, including Emma Watson,
John Boyega, and Tom Hanks.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:18.560
The plot centers on a creepy internet corporation
known as The Circle, which wants to create

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:20.780
a world where privacy is a thing of the past.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.400
Unfortunately, the film hits you right over
the head with its message.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:28.520
As The Atlantic put it, "It's all like an
episode of Black Mirror, if Black Mirror made

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.400
no effort whatsoever to be subtle."

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.440
The Emoji Movie

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.740
You might think a movie featuring Patrick

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:38.960
Stewart as a walking, talking piece of poop
would at least be worth watching as a gag,

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:43.900
but The Emoji Movie is such a soulless slog
it deprives you of even that simple pleasure.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.640
"You are smooth."

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:49.979
"Just doing my duty,"
It's a movie that's supposedly about being

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:54.720
true to yourself, but really, it's just a
big commercial for Spotify, Candy Crush, and

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:55.220
Sony.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:59.280
A lot of people scoffed at the idea of this
movie when it was first announced, and rightfully

00:04:59.280 --> 00:04:59.780
so.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:04.100
The film was obliterated by critics, even
though it still turned a profit at the box

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.600
office, because kids are the worst.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:08.980
"Look, tiny riot gear"

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:15.200
Birth of the Dragon

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.540
Making a movie about Bruce Lee should be the
easiest thing in the world.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:23.540
He was a martial arts master with a rags-to-riches
story, a truckload of charisma, and a tragic

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:24.040
demise.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:29.520
It's the perfect recipe for an awesome bio-pic,
but unfortunately, director George Nolfi ended

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:33.830
up making the worst kung fu flick of 2017
with Birth of the Dragon.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:39.280
"You have offended my family, and you have
offended the Shaolin temple."

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:44.160
Dragon centers on the infamous 1964 showdown
between Lee and Wong Jack Man.

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:48.551
Only instead of focusing on either of these
legendary figures, the movie spends way too

00:05:48.551 --> 00:05:53.349
much time following a white guy named Steve
who trains with Lee, sympathizes with Wong,

00:05:53.349 --> 00:05:55.980
and wants to save his Chinese girlfriend from
a crime boss.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:58.040
This isn't the movie anyone paid to see.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:03.120
Worse still, the film portrays Lee as an egocentric
jerk who needs a good beating, which is a

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.820
weird way to depict one of the most likable
movie stars of all time.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.600
Daddy's Home 2

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.640
When the original Daddy's Home hit theaters

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:16.060
in 2016, it scored a measly 31 percent approval
rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.040
So why make a sequel, and why release it during
the holidays?

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:21.160
Simply put, because of the money.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:22.960
That's what Christmas is all about.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:24.240
"He's fired?

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:26.860
But it's Christmas!"

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:28.440
"Thank you!"

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:33.460
Daddy's Home 2 picks up with Brad and Dusty
having become BFFs and excellent co-dads,

00:06:33.469 --> 00:06:36.460
but the status quo is torn apart when the
grandpas show up.

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:39.680
There's Brad's dad, who keeps kissing his
grownup son on the lips, and then there's

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:41.880
Dusty's old man, a womanizing jerk.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:46.199
With its painful holiday humor, Daddy's Home
2 is the kind of movie that might inspire

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:49.540
a new generation of Grinches to swear off
Christmas for good.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:50.800
The Shack

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:54.160
In 2007, author William P. Young published

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:57.560
The Shack, a best-selling novel about grief,
guilt, and God.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:02.820
Ten years later, it was turned into a movie
starring Sam Worthington, Octavia Spencer,

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:07.039
and Tim McGraw, and — spoiler alert — one
of those actors literally plays God.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:11.620
Variety summed it up as "a Hallmark-card therapy
session," which is putting it nicely.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:15.740
If you're looking for deep truths about religion,
you'd be better off looking just about anywhere

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:16.260
else.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:21.159
"So Always look on the bright side of passed."

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:28.420
Nope, you won't find any answers to life's
big questions here — unless you wanted to

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.960
know if God is a Neil Young fan.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.860
Second spoiler alert: yup.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:36.140
On the other hand, you will get to see Sam
Worthington race Jesus across a lake.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:36.780
So there's that.

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:38.040
The House

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:40.520
You can hire all the comedians you want, but

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.540
if you don't have a solid script, then your
movie won't get any laughs.

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:47.980
That was the problem with The House, the latest
from Andrew Jay Cohen and Brendan O'Brien

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.540
of Neighbors and Mike and Dave Need Wedding
Dates fame.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.680
Although The House boasts the talents of Will
Ferrell and Amy Poehler, instead of giving

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:57.540
them a strong screenplay to work with …
"Which we were kinda counting on…"

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:00.740
...it leans almost exclusively on their improv
skills.

00:08:00.749 --> 00:08:04.759
The so-called "comedy" revolves around a pair
of parents who open a casino in their friend's

00:08:04.759 --> 00:08:09.319
house to raise tuition money for their daughter,
but things spin wildly out of control.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:13.680
Soon, the two become suburbanite mobsters,
using drugs and chopping off fingers.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.419
While it seems like this wacky premise could
lead to some good gags, most of the jokes

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:21.420
failed to land with critics or those few audience
members who bothered to watch.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:22.520
Bright

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:24.880
Theoretically, Bright sounds like it should

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:25.879
be pretty awesome.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:29.840
A cop movie set in an alternate universe where
orcs and humans live side by side?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.099
Yeah, it sounds goofy, but it sounds like
the right kind of goofy.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:37.360
But while there's a rich mythology here to
explore, the world of Bright feels incredibly

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:38.380
two-dimensional.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:42.810
The action scenes lack any real spark, and
while Joel Edgerton tries to salvage the film

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:46.990
with the best performance he can muster under
all that orc makeup, the script isn't doing

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:48.010
him any favors.

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:50.580
Plus, whenever Will Smith starts dropping
lines like this…

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.459
"Fairy lives don't matter today."

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:57.640
...it's probably time to press pause and revisit…pretty
much anything else on Netflix.

00:08:58.240 --> 00:08:59.360
All Eyez on Me

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:02.100
Tupac Shakur was one of the most influential

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:06.320
artists of his generation, and he definitely
deserved a better bio-pic than All Eyez on

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:06.820
Me.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:11.140
The movie glosses heavily over the rapper's
career, hitting the basic highlights instead

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:12.700
of really digging into his life.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:17.720
As many critics have pointed out, the film
plays more like a Wikipedia page than an actual

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:18.220
movie.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:22.800
Here's hoping that one day, some future filmmaker
will make a Tupac movie that delves a bit

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.340
deeper into the artist's life.

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:26.100
Flatliners

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.180
When the original Flatliners dropped into

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:33.470
theaters back in 1990, it made a pretty penny
at the box office, but still failed to impress

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:34.340
many critics.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:39.500
Compared to 2017's pseudo-sequel, though,
the original feels like an absolute masterpiece

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:40.140
of horror.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:43.940
The film follows a group of med students experimenting
with life after life.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:47.900
Their tests involve taking some heavy duty
drugs, stopping their hearts for a minute

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:51.440
or two, and checking out the other side before
being resuscitated.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:55.940
Naturally, messing around with the afterlife
has serious consequences, but when our heroes

00:09:55.940 --> 00:10:00.900
starts experiencing some "spooky" visions,
the film devolves into Jump Scare: The Movie.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:06.060
Critics called out the film's lack of suspense,
foolish characters, and lacking visuals, leading

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:10.040
many to wish the property would've just stayed
where it belonged: in the afterlife.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.320
Thanks for watching!

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:14.220
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.500
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

